---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import EolBadge from "~/components/EolBadge.astro";
import StatusBadge from "~/components/StatusBadge.astro";
import { formatDate, loadEnrichedImages } from "~/lib/images";
import { loadBuildStatus, UNKNOWN_RUN, type RunInfo } from "~/lib/status";

const title = "Image freshness and build status";
const description =
  "Latest version, build date and age of every Open Image Cloud image, with the result of its last release and upstream watch runs. Rebuilt daily.";

/** Older than this, a row is highlighted (fine as long as upstream has not released). */
const STALE_DAYS = 45;
const RECENT_DAYS = 7;
const DAY_MS = 86_400_000;

const now = new Date();
const images = await loadEnrichedImages();
const status = await loadBuildStatus(images.map((i) => i.repo));

const rows = images.map((image) => {
  const repo = status.repos.get(image.repo);
  const release = repo?.release ?? UNKNOWN_RUN;
  const watch = repo?.watch ?? UNKNOWN_RUN;
  const built = image.builtAt ? new Date(image.builtAt) : null;
  const age =
    built && !Number.isNaN(built.getTime())
      ? Math.max(0, Math.floor((now.getTime() - built.getTime()) / DAY_MS))
      : null;
  const bump = status.bumps?.get(image.repo) ?? null;
  return {
    image,
    age,
    stale: age != null && age > STALE_DAYS,
    release,
    watch,
    bump,
    failed: release.state === "failure" || watch.state === "failure",
  };
});

const recent = rows.filter((r) => r.age != null && r.age <= RECENT_DAYS).length;
const failed = rows.filter((r) => r.failed).length;
const stale = rows.filter((r) => r.stale).length;
const eolCount = rows.filter((r) => r.image.support?.isEol).length;
const eolSoonCount = rows.filter((r) => r.image.support?.eolSoon).length;
const asOf = now.toISOString().replace(/\.\d{3}Z$/, "Z");
const asOfLabel = `${now.toISOString().slice(0, 10)} ${now.toISOString().slice(11, 16)} UTC`;

const RUN_LABELS: Record<RunInfo["state"], { label: string; cls: string }> = {
  success: { label: "Passed", cls: "text-ok" },
  failure: { label: "Failed", cls: "text-bad font-medium" },
  cancelled: { label: "Cancelled", cls: "text-ink-muted" },
  running: { label: "Running", cls: "text-accent" },
  none: { label: "None", cls: "text-ink-faint" },
  unknown: { label: "Unknown", cls: "text-ink-faint" },
};

const plural = (n: number, word: string) => `${n} ${word}${n === 1 ? "" : "s"}`;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: title,
    description,
    url: "https://openimages.cloud/status/",
    dateModified: asOf,
    isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "Open Image Cloud", url: "https://openimages.cloud/" },
  }}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">Status</p>
    <h1 class="text-ink mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{title}</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-pretty">
      When each image was last built, and how the last runs of its repository went: the release
      workflow (build, boot test, signature, publication) and the daily upstream watch, which opens
      a pull request when upstream publishes a new version. The support column is the end of
      upstream security support of the release, from endoflife.date. As of{" "}
      <time datetime={asOf} class="text-ink font-medium">
        {asOfLabel}
      </time>
      ; this page is rebuilt once a day.
    </p>

    <p class="border-line surface-sunken text-ink mt-8 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 text-sm">
      <strong class="font-semibold">{plural(rows.length, "image")}</strong>
      <span class="text-ink-faint mx-2" aria-hidden="true">
        ·
      </span>
      {recent} built in the last {RECENT_DAYS} days
      <span class="text-ink-faint mx-2" aria-hidden="true">
        ·
      </span>
      <span class:list={[failed > 0 && "text-bad font-medium"]}>
        {failed} with a failed last run
      </span>
      {eolCount + eolSoonCount > 0 && (
        <>
          <span class="text-ink-faint mx-2" aria-hidden="true">
            ·
          </span>
          <span class="text-warn">
            {eolCount > 0 && `${eolCount} past upstream end of life`}
            {eolCount > 0 && eolSoonCount > 0 && ", "}
            {eolSoonCount > 0 && `${eolSoonCount} reaching it within 6 months`}
          </span>
        </>
      )}
      {stale > 0 && (
        <>
          <span class="text-ink-faint mx-2" aria-hidden="true">
            ·
          </span>
          <span class="text-warn">
            {stale} built more than {STALE_DAYS} days ago
          </span>
        </>
      )}
    </p>

    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed">
      An old build is not a problem in itself: an image is rebuilt when upstream releases, and some
      distributions publish a few times a year. Age is highlighted after {STALE_DAYS} days so it can
      be checked against the upstream column; a failed run is what needs attention.
      {status.bumps == null && (
        <> The upstream column is unknown in this build: GitHub did not answer.</>
      )}
    </p>

    <div class="border-line mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[60rem] text-left text-sm">
        <caption class="sr-only">
          Build freshness and last workflow runs of each image, as of{asOfLabel}
        </caption>
        <thead class="surface-sunken border-line border-b">
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 font-normal">
              Image
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 font-normal">
              Latest
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 font-normal">
              Built
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 text-right font-normal">
              Age
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 font-normal">
              Upstream
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 font-normal">
              Supported until
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 font-normal">
              Last release
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="eyebrow px-4 py-2.5 font-normal">
              Last watch
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-line divide-y">
          {rows.map((r) => (
            <tr
              class:list={[
                r.failed && "bg-[color-mix(in_oklch,var(--bad)_7%,transparent)]",
                !r.failed && r.stale && "bg-[color-mix(in_oklch,var(--warn)_7%,transparent)]",
              ]}
            >
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-normal">
                <a
                  class="text-ink hover:text-accent font-medium"
                  href={`/images/${r.image.os_name}/`}
                >
                  {r.image.title}
                </a>
                {r.image.status !== "stable" && (
                  <span class="ml-2 align-middle">
                    <StatusBadge status={r.image.status} />
                  </span>
                )}
              </th>
              <td class="text-ink-muted px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">{r.image.latest_version}</td>
              <td class="text-ink-muted px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap">
                {r.image.builtAt ? (
                  <time datetime={r.image.builtAt}>{formatDate(r.image.builtAt)}</time>
                ) : (
                  "unknown"
                )}
              </td>
              <td
                class:list={[
                  "px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono text-xs whitespace-nowrap",
                  r.stale ? "text-warn font-medium" : "text-ink-muted",
                ]}
              >
                {r.age == null ? "?" : `${r.age} d`}
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">
                {r.bump ? (
                  <a class="link" href={r.bump.url} title={r.bump.title}>
                    New version pending
                  </a>
                ) : status.bumps == null ? (
                  <span class="text-ink-faint">Unknown</span>
                ) : r.watch.state === "success" ? (
                  <span class="text-ink-muted">No newer release</span>
                ) : r.watch.state === "none" ? (
                  <span class="text-ink-faint">Not watched</span>
                ) : (
                  <span class="text-ink-faint">Unknown</span>
                )}
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap">
                {r.image.support?.securityUntil ? (
                  <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
                    <a
                      class="text-ink-muted hover:underline"
                      href={r.image.support.sourceUrl}
                      title={`Release ${r.image.support.release}, from endoflife.date`}
                    >
                      {formatDate(r.image.support.securityUntil)}
                    </a>
                    <EolBadge support={r.image.support} />
                  </span>
                ) : r.image.support?.followsReleases ? (
                  <span class="text-ink-muted">Follows releases</span>
                ) : (
                  <span class="text-ink-faint">n/a</span>
                )}
              </td>
              {[r.release, r.watch].map((run) => (
                <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap">
                  {run.url ? (
                    <a
                      class:list={["hover:underline", RUN_LABELS[run.state].cls]}
                      href={run.url}
                      title={run.at ? `Started ${run.at}` : undefined}
                    >
                      {RUN_LABELS[run.state].label}
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    <span class={RUN_LABELS[run.state].cls}>{RUN_LABELS[run.state].label}</span>
                  )}
                  {run.at && (
                    <span class="text-ink-faint ml-1.5 text-xs">{formatDate(run.at)}</span>
                  )}
                </td>
              ))}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <ul class="text-ink-muted mt-6 max-w-3xl list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink">Built</strong> comes from the signed manifest of the latest
        version; age is counted from it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink">Upstream</strong>: "New version pending" links to the pull request
        the watcher opened; merging it publishes the release. Images built per OpenStack series
        (Octavia amphora) have no watcher.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink">Last release</strong> is the last run of the release workflow on a
        version tag or on main (runs on test branches are left out);{" "}
        <strong class="text-ink">Last watch</strong> the last daily upstream check. FreeBSD 14 and
        15 share one repository. "Unknown" means the GitHub API did not answer at build time.
      </li>
      <li>
        How each image is tested before it is published:{" "}
        <a class="link" href="/quality/">
          quality
        </a>
        . Release history of each image: its{" "}
        <a class="link" href="/feed.xml">
          Atom feed
        </a>
        .
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
